umbers that reinforcements isn't an issue for a while, and they can gather the unclaimed Chih-mei and train them.<br /> <br /> The Kindred seem wary of the Wan Gui, and a lot of the Wan Gui encounters seems to be ambushes or accidental mishaps.<br /> <br /> California is weakened because the Anarch Freestates fought and claimed it and Wan Gui have the element of Surprise. They likely had spies gathering intel before they arrived. But after they arrive its a system of push and pull to claim City Territory from the Kinjin, build Dragon's nests out of nodes, or steal caerns and convert it to dragons nests. They probably want to set up a system of accord with the Namebreakers and the Tribes of the Ferocious people, but the Deals with Kinjin are truces at best as they move their boundary lines farther and farther.<br /> <br /> But if they succeed they eventually have Dragon Nests and a place to Hemorrhage their excess population, as kind of western expanse, but really they are just traveling further east. But they ideally will establish courts in prime coastal cities, and this will give them greater leverage in dealing with the Kinjin, and it will probably start safer away from their homeland enemies the Yama Kings, but they will probably make new enemies as their realigning of Dragonlines converts the Near Umbra. Maybe they will war with Pentex?<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Recommendations? I need to read what was the California book San Francisco By Night, or was it LA by Night? <br /> <br /> <br /> Come on I think this is salvageable if we just jimmy with the setting a bit and make assumptions like an overpopulation of the Dead. Aslo they started this initiative while they were winning their struggle in India, but then the Ravnos used Mass Embrace tactics and Zapathsura Wokee up and yada Yada everything within a few hundred Miles of Bangladesh has a screwy nervous supernatural population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments"