u5927\u8dc3\u5916( The Great Leap Outward, which may come from the infamous political activity \u201c\u5927\u8dc3\u8fdb (The Great Leap Forward)\u201d ) is a foolish, cunning and racist ops which is doomed to fail, the Shadow War even implies this.<br /> <br /> Wan Gui pupils go abroad to battle the gwelio just because of their foolish racism (We noble wan gui are bigger than you, Kin Jin!)<br /> <br /> They don\u2019t have many disadvantages on number, resupply, powers, organizaion. They can only kick the Anarch, but Camarilla and Sabbat? AFAIK, very poor results<br /> <br /> They know few about their rivals (maybe they don\u2019t even know monsters Helena or Menele or Sybil which equal to their mightiest masters)<br /> <br /> Their elders acquiescence them, sentencing them to death, because of political benefits<br /> <br /> WW injected Yellow Peril, Racism and so on, which are very common but now out of date<br /> <br /> Make me recall The Boxer Rebellion, stupid and poor people!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-08-2020, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:17:07-07:00","id":1379857,"title":"","content":"\u201cMy roommate. Dante Pignetti.\u201d \ud83d\ude22<br /> <br /> Also Penelope (not me, the other one)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:58:50-07:00","id":1379872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1379459#post1379459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Overpopulation as a reason doesn't really work for Hungry Ghosts, if you get too many Chih Mei, unlikely as its a rare soul that makes its way back, you just chain them up as extra guard dogs and never let them regain their mental faculties.</div> </div> </div> </div>This^<br /> <br /> Overpopulation doesn't need to be dealt with any subtlety in Kue-Jin society. It's not like the Kindred, where the excess vampires are mostly the progeny of older vampires who will get pissed and maneuver against you if you openly kill their precious widdle baby bloodsucker. Newborns just pop up randomly, and you can dispose of them openly without consequence.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T01:05:20-07:00","id":1380052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense#post1379442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So like the title says lets make the Great Leap Outwards make sense!<br /> <br /> The biggest problem being Wan Gui can't embrace, they have to find those Zombie form first risen and train them to civility outside of their Chih-Mei mindset.<br /> <br /> So to fix it perhaps the Wan Gui are experiencing a sever degree of overpopulation.<br /> <br /> Maybe they discovered a greater amount of Chih-Mei appear if the Wan Gui Set up courts around Dragon Nests in cities and populations in the west but with Asian populations. Maybe Dragon Nests sort of calibrate and synchronize nearby Penumbra and Shadowlands into more of the Yin and Yang realm order of their homeland.<br /> <br /> <br /> So lets say they are experiencing a population boost, they don't have enough prime real-estate for everyone. It would cause a lot of problems to keep everyone fighting for the established positions in the tradition cities, meanwhile they get reports some Chih may appear in places where immigrants gather and sort of set a bubble of consensus more aligned with the Middle Kingdom and the Mirrorlands. So they kill two birds with one stone and order the ambitious and much to populous next generation and experienced court members ,who want to a fresh city to claim a high position in. so they send them to Coastal populations to set footholds in the West. They send them in large enough numbers that reinforcements isn't an issue for a while, and they can gather the unclaimed Chih-mei and train them.<br /> <br /> The Kindred seem wary of the Wan Gui, and a lot of the Wan Gui encounters seems to be ambushes or accidental mishaps.<br /> <br /> California is weakened because the Anarch Freestates fought and claimed it and Wan Gui have the element of Surprise. They likely had spies gathering intel before they arrived. But after they arrive its a system of push and pull to claim City Territory from the Kinjin, build Dragon's nests out of nodes, or steal caerns and convert it to dragons nests. They probably want to set up a system of accord with the Namebreakers and the Tribes of the Ferocious people, but the Deals with Kinjin are truces at best as they move their boundary lines farther and farther.<br /> <br /> But if they succeed they eventually have Dragon Nests and a place to Hemorrhage their excess population, as kind of western expanse, but really they are just traveling further east. But they ideally will establish courts in prime coastal cities, and this will give them greater leverage in dealing with the Kinjin, and it will probably start safer away from their homeland enemies the Yama Kings, but they will probably make new enemies as their realigning of Dragonlines converts the Near Umbra. Maybe they will war with Pentex?<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Recommendations? I need to read what was the California book San Francisco By Night, or was it LA by Night?<br /> <br /> <br /> Come on I think this is salvageable if we just jimmy with the setting a bit and make assumptions like an overpopulation of the Dead. Aslo they started this initiative while they were winning their struggle in India, but then the Ravnos used Mass Embrace tactics and Zapathsura Wokee up and yada Yada everything within a few hundred Miles of Bangladesh has a screwy nervous supernatural population.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The assault is explained in Nights of Prophecy (Walking After Midnight scenario). The timeline is more or less like this, from first to last:<br /> <br /> 1998:<br /> - Invasion of LA (Ash Plan)<br /> - Conquest of Hong Kong (Two-Fang Serpent Plan)<br /> <br /> 1999:<br /> - (July) Eye of the Demon Emperor (Red Star)<br /> - (Friday, July 23, 1999) Ravnos Antediluvian awakens, beginning of the Week of Nightmares<br /> - (Sunday, July 25, 1999) Eight Thunder Sage, Rising Majestically and Black Earth Boy fight Zapathasura, he curses the entire Clan before his final death<br /> - Great storm struck Yellow Springs (Destruction of Enoch or Ends of Empire maelstrom?)<br /> - Failure of Ash Plan / Progress in Shanghai / Stalemate in Hong Kong<br /> - Alliance of Oliver Thrace<br /> - (late) Mandarin Hao Wei-Liang commits honorable suicide (facing the &quot;Eye of Heaven&quot;, the sun)<br /> <br /> 2000:<br /> - Jiejie Li gathers allies and go to LA<br /> - Offers aid to anarchs in exchange for eliminating their kinjin enemies<br /> - Alliance established and conquer of LA<br /> - Mme. Guil gather aid in Boston, then in San Francisco<br /> - Pact is proposed<br /> - Nights of Prophecy scenario<br /> <br /> The assault on the west coast itself is a giant F*** U planned by the Resplendent Cranes due to the British colonization during imperial times. Kueijin suffered the most during Mongol times, this was their Convention of Thorns equivalent in which they had to re-arrange themselves into a different organization, and now we have the Qincunx, the Uji and the Golden Courts. They heavily foreigners and having the British Empire conquer them is a wound that never healed. I guess that having US west coast as the target was an excuse to advance the metaplot in an already established setting like the by Nights of second edition, yet it delivered really good stories around the setting. The Great Leap Outward does make sense, its motives and procedure is explained throughout many books and that probably made it a bit confusing to follow.<br /> <br /> San Francisco by Night is probably the worst book for KotE. It was a shame that ignored almost everything on WoD 1st ed and Prince of the City, because it was a great opportunity to advance that setting and some distinguished NPCs like Vannevar Thomas and Sebastian Melmoth, but the writer simply chose to ignore them. The book also lacked most of the kindred history of the city (just like Jerusalem by Night, which was also very poor in cainite history).<br /> <br /> On Pentex, probably the Devil Tigers can be their best allies in the was against the changing breeds.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 04-10-2020, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T02:55:11-07:00","id":1380066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380052#post1380052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The assault on the west coast itself is a giant F*** U planned by the Resplendent Cranes due to the British colonization during imperial times. Kueijin suffered the most during Mongol times, this was their Convention of Thorns equivalent in which they had to re-arrange themselves into a different organization, and now we have the Qincunx, the Uji and the Golden Courts. They heavily foreigners and having the British Empire conquer them is a wound that never healed. I guess that having US west coast as the target was an excuse to advance the metaplot in an already established setting like the by Nights of second edition, yet it delivered really good stories around the setting. The Great Leap Outward does make sense, its motives and procedure is explained throughout many books and that probably made it a bit confusing to follow.<br /> <br /> San Francisco by Night is probably the worst book for KotE. It was a shame that ignored almost everything on WoD 1st ed and Prince of the City, because it was a great opportunity to advance that setting and some distinguished NPCs like Vannevar Thomas and Sebastian Melmoth, but the writer simply chose to ignore them. The book also lacked most of the kindred history of the city (just like Jerusalem by Night, which was also very poor in cainite history).<br /> <br /> On Pentex, probably the Devil Tigers can be their best allies in the was against the changing breeds.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, thats what happened but it still doesn't make sense unless your the kind of arsehole whose willing to destroy everyone younger than you in order to attack people who never did anything to you in the first place.....<br /> <br /> I mean every single Hungry Ghost who dies is a loss of a decade or so of investment, training and resources. Every Kindred that dies is the loss of.....a nights worth of investment to replace. And there are many, many more Kindred than Hungry Ghosts.<br /> <br /> It doesn't make sense logistically or culturally or really in any way.<br /> <br /> If the Quincunx had attacked the UK.....maybe.....it could be seen as an insane revenge plot that acheived nothing, attacking west coast US? Not so much.<br /> <br /> I mean we know the Quincunx don't give a fuck about any Hungry Ghosts outside their own court and any Hungry Ghost who isn't an Ancestor barely registers as a person for them but they basically just handed every single Dragon Nest that they personally are not squatting on over to the Shen and others and ceded even more territory for nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T06:09:31-07:00","id":1380098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380052#post1380052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> On Pentex, probably the Devil Tigers can be their best allies in the was against the changing breeds.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex and the Devil Tigers cannot coexist. The Tigers exist to punish the thralls of the Yama Kings, and the Yama Kings are beholden to the Wyrm whether they know it or not. The Tigers may use fire to fight fire, but they wont work with anything that smacks of the Wyrm. IMO anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T08:43:52-07:00","id":1380135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380098#post1380098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pentex and the Devil Tigers cannot coexist. The Tigers exist to punish the thralls of the Yama Kings, and the Yama Kings are beholden to the Wyrm whether they know it or not. The Tigers may use fire to fight fire, but they wont work with anything that smacks of the Wyrm. IMO anyway.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you, a modern high-tech devil-tiger sect even competed with Pentex and Mikaboshi in economy<br /> <br /> And Tigers just seem to be infernalist, at most. Their essence differ a lot from that<br /> <br /> *Btw, IMO I think wan gui is doomed to fail when competing with Yamas, they\u2019re creatures of hell, carrying the essence of hell (Po)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T12:29:12-07:00","id":1380175,"title":"","content":"yepp, Electic Money Wickedness Club was an amazing concept.<br /> <br /> I don't think Tigers could be squarely put under infernalist brand. Maybe self-infernalist would hit closer to home.<br /> <br /> The one but very important advantage they had over the Yama kings and their servants is that they had Hun while Yama servants either lacked it completely or buried it under millenia of sin (although a concept of awakening a Yama servant or even a Yama King's Hun akin to Spectre's awakening of Psyche defeating a Shadow and returning him/her to Wraith-state presents a very very tempting concept of redemption at Celestial-level, at least to me). Said Hun helps them to balance out the temptations and corruption of the Wyrm on their quest compared to those who forsook it in favor of submerging their soul in P'o. Seeing the universe solely through the eyes of the devil may be an advantage but also declines you so many alternatives and enslaves you to that vision. Getting into the skin of the demon using your P'o to understand and see through the ways of your enemy (Yama, Wyrm) while ultimately serving the goals of Hun' (Wyld/Weaver) is one of the biggest advantages of eastern Kindred as a whole compared to Cainites' clumsy efforts to fight off Baali and whatever other Wyrm/infernal threat they face. (with the recent introduction of Baali Molochim being a slight improvement)<br /> <br /> Another reason why I saw KotE setting a lesson long overdue to the VtM inhabitants. Shielding off against the 'baaad' side of things will only get you so far. Disciplining yourself in order to walk the line between understanding the monster within and without, and falling prey to it, is one hell of an improvement (pun intended).<br /> <br /> Once I read more metaplot on Werewolf, I got a better grip on the Devil-Tiger idea: they play the role of the Balancer Wyrm which was an inseparable part of the Triat and served the existence in cleansing it of it's sick or old elements while the corrupted Wyrm (corrupted, most obviously, by the Weaver, mind you) wishes to drown creation in things and concepts, most of which were born out of it's feverish nightmares. A 'healthy' world rid of the corrupt wyrm would have devil tigers tend to the mortal garden (much like the salubri of old did) and let things which have outgrown their time under the stars go for rebirth/recycle.<br /> <br /> Even the scorpion-eaters are not quite yama kings servants/infernalists, they serve the KotE metaplot as a symbol of the Sixth age and share many features (I'd say too many) with the Path of Night Lasombra from VtM - an ultimate petty criminal who just wants to get through bad times relatively intact to simply exist for as long as possible feeding off others' suffering and not doing much him/herself. Extremely bestial concept which, nevertheless, occupies a valuable niche of a cautionary tale in many chronicles. A tale about the consequences of going spiritually bankrupt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","user":"Val_Nir","date":". 04-10-2020, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T15:16:28-07:00","id":1380213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380098#post1380098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pentex and the Devil Tigers cannot coexist. The Tigers exist to punish the thralls of the Yama Kings, and the Yama Kings are beholden to the Wyrm whether they know it or not. The Tigers may use fire to fight fire, but they wont work with anything that smacks of the Wyrm. IMO anyway.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yama Kings beholden to Wyrm, where did that come from? Werewolf sourcebook? My take on Pentex and Devil Tigers working for together is on defilement of dragon nests or comparing notes in the bakemono creation department. They can probably have a sort of alliance for a small common goal from time to time.<br /> <br /> -. Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T15:48:14-07:00","id":1380221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380066#post1380066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, thats what happened but it still doesn't make sense unless your the kind of arsehole whose willing to destroy everyone younger than you in order to attack people who never did anything to you in the first place.....<br /> <br /> I mean every single Hungry Ghost who dies is a loss of a decade or so of investment, training and resources. Every Kindred that dies is the loss of.....a nights worth of investment to replace. And there are many, many more Kindred than Hungry Ghosts.<br /> <br /> It doesn't make sense logistically or culturally or really in any way.<br /> <br /> If the Quincunx had attacked the UK.....maybe.....it could be seen as an insane revenge plot that acheived nothing, attacking west coast US? Not so much.<br /> <br /> I mean we know the Quincunx don't give a fuck about any Hungry Ghosts outside their own court and any Hungry Ghost who isn't an Ancestor barely registers as a person for them but they basically just handed every single Dragon Nest that they personally are not squatting on over to the Shen and others and ceded even more territory for nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess what happened was more of a why and when, rather that the logistical process of it. PRC recently got handed HK and they just recovered from a Shanghai akuma infested territory. After being limited in territory for centuries, now is the moment of them to expand further.<br /> <br /> As I said above, the decision on using the US west coast was due to using already familiar setting within the game rather than logical. If it was me doing it, I'd let the Qincunx strike the British colonies (or ex-) first. New Zealand, Australia, Canada would be the main targets, and then attack England itself. They might surely know of Sundervere who almost killed Mithras once, perhaps get some pointers from him first.<br /> <br /> Then I think on the why San Francisco and LA first. Mainly it does have an interesting chinese historical background, something the British colonial territories lack. After a century or so, perhaps it was that very thing the reason why now kanbujian exist in such territories. Second Breath is a specific procedure to asian territories and now they are beginning to appear elsewhere, specifically places with huge chinese immigration (California).<br /> <br /> Perhaps this is their endgame (if you ignore the Sixth Age scenario). China now have established immigration in almost every country in the world (50+ millions). Notable places are USA, Canada, Peru, Australia, France, South Africa and the United Kingdom. Their immigration could have triggered the kanbujian effect into every chinatown in the world, this would expand their numbers massively.<br /> <br /> That might be the reason why the send the first wave to die. &quot;Kindred, this is not an attack, this is a message of what's coming. We have the numbers and they are continually growing.&quot; and the next attack will be everywhere from within the cities. It has always been a long term plan.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T16:06:33-07:00","id":1380228,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3399_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3399\" data-vbnamecard=\"3399\">hachiman</a> totally agree","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T18:34:58-07:00","id":1380259,"title":"","content":"An idea I came up with as a headcanon.<br /> <br /> <b>The Great Leap Outward Betrayal</b><br /> <br /> By. Beckett<br /> <br /> There's no actual conflict between the Camarilla and the Quincunx. Quite the contrary, they have been at peace for the better part of a few centuries with diplomats sent by the Inner Council almost immediately after the Convention of Thorns that were greeted with welcoming arms. This is almost in complete contradiction to the assumption that all Kindred who journey East will be killed. In truth, such is only likely to happen if you don't bring any gifts or pay the proper respects. The Camarilla and Quincunx have a long-standing &quot;strong fences make good neighbors&quot; policy that primarily exists to keep younger Kindred in line.<br /> <br /> So why the ignominiously named &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot;? Well, the truth of that matter is that it was entirely the work of Justicars Cock Robin and Lucinde working with a number of highly ranked Devil Tigers. In simple terms, the Great Leap Outward was a cruel and vicious backroom deal designed to eradicate the Anarch Free States.<br /> <br /> The Wan Kuei were paid extremely large sums of money and there's some question that Queen Anne Bowesley made sure the Chinese takeover of Hong Kong went without a hitch for their part in the story: they were to beat the drum of war and talk about the White Devils that needed to be purged from California before sending an army of young soldiers to slaughter the Anarch-dominated territory. It was an immensely cynical ploy that was designed to take advantage of the fact that the number of younger Wan Kuei had exploded, the lack of spiritual balance following WW2 and communist China [atheism not affecting the number of undead but affecting their loyalty to ancient Chinese warlords], and needed to be pruned.<br /> <br /> The Wan Kuei invaders were never meant to hold the territory they acquired and it was, in simple terms, as nasty a frontline assassination as Uriah the Hittite. It was, initially, a smashing success as the number of Anarchs in California were reduced by half and some suggested even more. Certainly, the Anarch Free State seemed a thing of the past. Unfortunately, the Camarilla miscalculated by sending the venal Sebastian La Croix to &quot;claim&quot; Los Angeles even as the leader of the Wan Kuei, Ming Xiao, figured out that she had been sent to lead a crusade never meant to reach Jerusalem. The two ended up planning to betray their patrons, assassinated, and the Anarchs rallying around a new victory.<br /> <br /> Still, if the Anarchs endured and were pruned of dead weight, the Camarilla and Quincunx largely achieved its aims. They inflicted immense casualties on their enemies while barely lifting a finger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T19:01:50-07:00","id":1380264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense#post1379442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So like the title says lets make the Great Leap Outwards make sense!<br /> <br /> The biggest problem being Wan Gui can't embrace, they have to find those Zombie form first risen and train them to civility outside of their Chih-Mei mindset.<br /> <br /> So to fix it perhaps the Wan Gui are experiencing a sever degree of overpopulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the Great Leap Outward is most easily explained by ancient elders who don't like the modern world and hold &quot;the West&quot; as responsible for the Turning of the Wheel so for them, this is &quot;revenge&quot; (even if the place they're invading has nothing to do with what happened). Further, there are a lot more Wan Kuei than there used to be (due to basic population trends but also the fact that a greater percentage of souls end up in Yomi after death) and, of course, you have various hidden Akuma (some of whom might be those very ancient elders) trying to convince everyone that sending a bunch of young vampires off to die in America is a great idea. Because when you look at it, the only winner in the Great Leap Outward are the Yama Kings (lots of Wan Kuei off somewhere else means it's easier for them to amass power, plus with a lot of younger Wan Kuei seeing themselves getting thrown away like that, more opportunities to tempt them into becoming servants of Yomi).<br /> <br /> Ultimately the Great Leap Outward is viewed by many Wan Kuei as a terrible idea, but it's got enough support to go through and there are a lot of younger vampires who are on board with it because it gives them the chance to go off and be heroes and make big names for themselves, which would be a lot harder if they stayed at home.<br /> <br /> Even those who don't necessarily like or agree with it find themselves forced to sort of help out a bit or risk being branded as traitors or even akuma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T21:53:08-07:00","id":1380306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1379456#post1379456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view is that it's a scam on younger Kuei-Jin.<br /> <br /> They sent them on a racist Crusade into California to get killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also helped to create chaos among the filthy western vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T15:47:09-07:00","id":1380506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380213#post1380213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yama Kings beholden to Wyrm, where did that come from? Werewolf sourcebook? My take on Pentex and Devil Tigers working for together is on defilement of dragon nests or comparing notes in the bakemono creation department. They can probably have a sort of alliance for a small common goal from time to time.<br /> <br /> -. Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Yama Kings and the Yomi Wan are basically Maeljin and Malfeas.<br /> While methods of both dharma and Pentex are the same, their ultimate goals are not just different, they contradict each other. Helping Pentex in any way would be like helping akuma. If anything, Tigers would better retake defiled nests from Pentex by force and guard the secrets of bakemono creation from it. I get your idea on occasional cooperation, but Pentex is an ultimate competitor to them. Not sure if any kind of cooperation could happen on any level higher than individual, personal-need alliance, and even then black iron talons would probably like to have a word or two with such a tiger.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T17:31:20-07:00","id":1380521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380506#post1380506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yama Kings and the Yomi Wan are basically Maeljin and Malfeas.<br /> While methods of both dharma and Pentex are the same, their ultimate goals are not just different, they contradict each other. Helping Pentex in any way would be like helping akuma. If anything, Tigers would better retake defiled nests from Pentex by force and guard the secrets of bakemono creation from it. I get your idea on occasional cooperation, but Pentex is an ultimate competitor to them. Not sure if any kind of cooperation could happen on any level higher than individual, personal-need alliance, and even then black iron talons would probably like to have a word or two with such a tiger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of why the Kindred of the East are hard to play is they're the lesser evil and don't quite fit the WOD.<br /> <br /> Sort of like the Mages and Changelings.<br /> <br /> Antihero for life.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T18:04:39-07:00","id":1380527,"title":"","content":"It makes sense, KJ society pre 19th century imperialism is.. MUCH less racist. Much like Modern Kindred society is functionally run by the Ancilla the big group of people running KJ society as of the 20th century are....people who died in the 19th century. They still hold their grudges and... the Anarch freestate was setup to fall.<br /> <br /> That the Camarilla or Sabbat didn't Take the territory in kind after the KJ expended their load is really the issue. Assuming the Free state fell in the late 90s There should be a completely new status quo by 2020. Maybe the KJ make a Deal with one side, have their &quot;Promise&quot; equivalent and sell most of the territory to the winner.. maybe they get smashed out and then the other side makes the deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T18:12:43-07:00","id":1380530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380521#post1380521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of why the Kindred of the East are hard to play is they're the lesser evil and don't quite fit the WOD.<br /> <br /> Sort of like the Mages and Changelings.<br /> <br /> Antihero for life.</div> </div> </div> </div>KotE are not solely devil-tigers. There are other four mainstream dharmas + 5 heretical ones. While devil-tigers and their nest reek of Wyrm, resplendant cranes shine ice-cold with the energy of the Weaver, and the thrashing dragons bubble with Wyld.<br /> <br /> No, they are not hard to play. One of the most interesting - certainly. Along with Sabbat, Technocracy, Tal'Mahe'Ra, Uktena etc. Tbh, any splat's faction, even the more 'mainstream' ones, are hard to play, with a right set of tools at storyteller's disposal.<br /> <br /> WoD is all about lesser and greater evils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T19:12:42-07:00","id":1380544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380530#post1380530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> KotE are not solely devil-tigers. There are other four mainstream dharmas + 5 heretical ones. While devil-tigers and their nest reek of Wyrm, resplendant cranes shine ice-cold with the energy of the Weaver, and the thrashing dragons bubble with Wyld.<br /> <br /> No, they are not hard to play. One of the most interesting - certainly. Along with Sabbat, Technocracy, Tal'Mahe'Ra, Uktena etc. Tbh, any splat's faction, even the more 'mainstream' ones, are hard to play, with a right set of tools at storyteller's disposal.<br /> <br /> WoD is all about lesser and greater evils.</div> </div> </div> </div>Devil Tigers are also far less likely to get involved with the GLO, given what the Dharma book had to say on the subject in the main-line V:tM crossover section (&quot;Leave 'kill whitey' to the Resplendent Cranes&quot;). They're far too busy tempting and punishing sinners to bother with counter-imperialism, and their philosophy is also generally counter to the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T23:13:02-07:00","id":1380587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380530#post1380530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they are not hard to play. One of the most interesting - certainly. Along with Sabbat, Technocracy, Tal'Mahe'Ra, Uktena etc. Tbh, any splat's faction, even the more 'mainstream' ones, are hard to play, with a right set of tools at storyteller's disposal.<br /> <br /> WoD is all about lesser and greater evils.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do find Wan Kuei are a bit harder to play than some character types - playing one is like playing a Kindred on a Path or a Road instead of just rolling with basic Humanity. And that sort of playstyle isn't for everyone, and I can get why some people wouldn't be able to grok playing that sort of character. On the other hand that's exactly why I find them interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T02:29:16-07:00","id":1380606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380587#post1380587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do find Wan Kuei are a bit harder to play than some character types - playing one is like playing a Kindred on a Path or a Road instead of just rolling with basic Humanity. And that sort of playstyle isn't for everyone, and I can get why some people wouldn't be able to grok playing that sort of character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yepp, apologies for my rather categorical statement. Your correction stands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand that's exactly why I find them interesting. </div> </div> </div>I totally and wholeheartedly agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Devil Tigers are also far less likely to get involved with the GLO, given what the Dharma book had to say on the subject in the main-line V:tM crossover section (&quot;Leave 'kill whitey' to the Resplendent Cranes&quot;). They're far too busy tempting and punishing sinners to bother with counter-imperialism, and their philosophy is also generally counter to the concept. </div> </div> </div>Yes, while Cranes' book has a whole section dedicated to their plans not only for the US but for other parts of the world too, &quot;Devil-Tigers see the Leap as equivalent of weeding the garden while your house is on fire.&quot;(c)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T06:31:03-07:00","id":1380644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380213#post1380213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yama Kings beholden to Wyrm, where did that come from? Werewolf sourcebook? My take on Pentex and Devil Tigers working for together is on defilement of dragon nests or comparing notes in the bakemono creation department. They can probably have a sort of alliance for a small common goal from time to time.<br /> <br /> -. Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's in Thousan Hells. The force underlying the Yama Kings is &quot;The Centipede&quot; which is analogous to the Wyrm. It's an attempt at crossover. The Devil Tiger apotheosis is to become a Righteous Yama King who releases souls from Hell when they have served their time in it. They fight fire with fire, they are not servants of evil and corruption.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:23:50-07:00","id":1380694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380644#post1380644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's in Thousan Hells. The force underlying the Yama Kings is &amp;quot;The Centipede&amp;quot; which is analogous to the Wyrm. It's an attempt at crossover. The Devil Tiger apotheosis is to become a Righteous Yama King who releases souls from Hell when they have served their time in it. They fight fire with fire, they are not servants of evil and corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hengeyokai Book and Player Guide to the Changing Breeds also apply. Yams Kings are powerful banes in garou term, and Incarnas are Ministers of the Heaven","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:06:36-07:00","id":1380726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380644#post1380644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's in Thousan Hells. The force underlying the Yama Kings is &quot;The Centipede&quot; which is analogous to the Wyrm. It's an attempt at crossover. The Devil Tiger apotheosis is to become a Righteous Yama King who releases souls from Hell when they have served their time in it. They fight fire with fire, they are not servants of evil and corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>1000 Hells only mentions a kind of tale that features the Wyrm as a clumsy Great Dragon that was terribly embarrassed at having tripped and fallen into the weave of the world, breaking it, and thereafter began hiding from everything because of the loss of face. This is one of those &quot;sort of true, through someone else's eyes&quot; things. If one takes both the imprisonment of the Wyrm and the notion of primordial corruption related to negative emotions at face value, it suggests that both those hells and the Wyrm ended up getting spattered with nasty gunk that was leftover from the creation of the cosmos, and in some fashion, are either addicted to it or can't escape from it. The Bastet label that Asura, and regard it and bane-spirits as separate from the Wyrm proper.<br /> <br /> Whether or not the Yama Kings believe that they serve it, though, is immaterial. As a form of elemental corruption, it doesn't require conscious acknowledgment of it as a specific force. It only &quot;cares&quot; that people choose to do ill, and it exists where they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T17:24:21-07:00","id":1380796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380726#post1380726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1000 Hells only mentions a kind of tale that features the Wyrm as a clumsy Great Dragon</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of this, iirc The Centipede always refers to the Wyrm in Middle Kingdom, the Great Dragon refers to Zmei, at least in Blood &amp; Silk,<br /> <br /> B&amp;S, Page 23<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The chaos of ever-changing sovereignty in the north concealed an epic series of spirit battles, as a number of packs of Xiong Ren subdued and chained a Great Dragon in the forest of the far northern wasteland. This creature strains at its bond even today, I am told. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T18:00:51-07:00","id":1380809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1380796#post1380796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of this, iirc The Centipede always refers to the Wyrm in Middle Kingdom, the Great Dragon refers to Zmei, at least in Blood &amp; Silk,<br /> <br /> B&amp;S, Page 23</div> </div> </div> </div>Everywhere but in the passage from The 1000 Hells and the Kitsune portion of Hengeyokai.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T14:54:48-07:00","id":1382828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1379872#post1379872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This^<br /> <br /> Overpopulation doesn't need to be dealt with any subtlety in Kue-Jin society. It's not like the Kindred, where the excess vampires are mostly the progeny of older vampires who will get pissed and maneuver against you if you openly kill their precious widdle baby bloodsucker. Newborns just pop up randomly, and you can dispose of them openly without consequence.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait I thought this was all frowned upon. I thought, much like the Settites, they were obligated to let fellow escapes from hell have a chance at Dharmic absolution, like its something all 5 Dharmas would agree on, and if someone is found to just be killing them willy nilly or hiding them away as beastial thralls and the rest of Wan Gui Society found out they would be very upset. Like with Setites you are allowed to manipulate and corrupt mortals and vampires for your own benefit but ultimately if you are not steering peoples Souls to Liberation through unshackling of the Chains placed upon them by the Aeons you are considered a heinous dick by the rest of the Cult of Set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T15:10:02-07:00","id":1382830,"title":"","content":"Yeah. While it's possible older vampires would kill newly born Wan Kuei out of hand, doing that on any large scale action would likely get the elder branded as Akuma. I mean, the Wan Kuei are in an existential war for existence against the Yama Kings, so just offing your reinforcements because you're worried about your political position isn't going to fly. In fact, it's the kind of thing I expect if the Yama Kings found out about it, they could blackmail that elder into slowly becoming an Akuma for real by threatening to release the list of other Wan Kuei they've killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T20:11:14-07:00","id":1382885,"title":"","content":"Maybe the folks behind the Great Leap Outward are in fact akuma? Or they could be made so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T21:03:53-07:00","id":1382890,"title":"","content":"Eh, Devil Tigers keep the Chih-Mei of their old enemies families as pets and guard dogs. Thrashing Dragons use them as court decorations. Whose to say they won't eventually get around to waking them? Either way a sudden abundance of Hungry Ghosts babies is an unusual occurrence compared to the headaches caused by mass embraces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-n