":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T04:29:30-07:00","id":1382950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1382911#post1382911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This would actually be hilarious. Like they send the Will Ferrell of the Kue-jin over there with Wu of flunkies, and like two montages and a dick joke later, they've bumbled their way into utterly dominating the Bay Area and are slowly squashing the rest of the Anarch Free State.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, it would explain why they made such incredibly bad deals and eventually lost California.<br /> <br /> San Fransisco vampire: Oh thank you! We're so glad you're here. Vannevar Thomas is an awful Prince and we are glad to be liberated from him.<br /> <br /> Kuei-Jin: Silence! We are imposing a state of MARTIAL LAW where all vampires must serve the Kuei-Jin.<br /> <br /> San Fransisco vampire: Uh, this isn't Nazi Germany. You don't even have control of the local authorities.<br /> <br /> Kuei-Jin: This will not backfire!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T04:33:09-07:00","id":1382951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1382945#post1382945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry I\u2019m not that humorous</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very confused.<br /> <br /> What does humour have to do with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 04-21-2020, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T05:17:50-07:00","id":1382959,"title":"","content":"By the time the Kindred of the East end of the world scenarios in &quot;Time of Judgement&quot; roll around, a number of wu on the American west coast have figured out that they've been had. The reinforcements that they need to occupy and secure the territories they've won are never coming.<br /> <br /> One can certainly go in a different direction with this if you want to play out a different scenario, but the canon timeline that ended in 2004 definitely seems to have been one where the elders were just disposing of excess newbies in order to avoid competition from ambitious young immortals, dharma and the search for ascension notwithstanding. It's very much an idealistic youngsters versus the corrupt older generation scenario, where the invading Kuei Jin ironically have much more in common with the Anarchs and Camarilla neonates than they have with the elders who sent them across the Pacific.<br /> <br /> It ends up not mattering in the end, because the dawning of the Sixth Age takes priority all of a sudden. I think that showing that the ancients can't be looked to for the necessary leadership to see the Kuei Jin through the threat of the Demon Emperor is very much in keeping with the mood and tone of the end of the world story that White Wolf wanted to tell at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 04-21-2020, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T06:57:33-07:00","id":1382969,"title":"","content":"I'm doing a San Francisco Chronicle, somewhat updated and with a cold war between the Keui-jin and Camarilla splitting control of the metro area. As I play it, at least one of the motivations for the Great Leap Outward was to secure territory among their expanding cultural groups so that they could intercede with Keui-jin who are taking their Second Breaths on the West Coast or other places such as Hong Kong that were under Camarilla control. So they are expanding to protect territories in which Keui-jin were now starting to be reborn into in significant numbers so that they could be inducted onto Dharmic paths. This is complicated by the unexpected discovery of Kanbujian existing in any numbers, which the Keui-jin see as an aberration they don't really know what to do with.<br /> <br /> As for why this movement was violent, the answer one of my NPCs gave was something akin to: &quot;The greatest and earliest emissary from the Western Kindred was Zao-Lat, the Betrayer, a thief, a despicable creature who benefited from their compassion and stole their wisdom (see the history of Saulot). Where the Keui-jin meet Western vampires in India, there is genocidal war spanning millennia (see the Ravnos write up), and in the previous centuries, when the Western colonial powers arrived, the Western Kindred came with to seize all they could. Why would we think that asking nicely would get us anywhere?&quot;<br /> <br /> I've also reinforced the first point with a house rule/fluff that western Vampire feeding in significant quantities fouls the chi in the area, making it more difficult for Keui-jin to feed on anything that is not Demon chi. There is some fluff text about western vampire feeding fouling chi in the Kindred of the East Companion, and I built this idea off of that. This makes it more difficult for newly risen Keui-jin to survive and master their Po's without being moved to protected areas free from this influence that are now maintained by the Keui-jin. This also motivates the Keui-jin to maintain separate territories and look dimly on Kindred intrusions, particularly feeding.<br /> <br /> I expand on this idea for Werewolf as well to help reinforce the traditional animosity between vampires and Garou, in that Kindred feeding creates a 'spiritual wound' on the victims that Bane spirits can exploit. So historically from the Garou's point of view, vampires have been parasitic harbingers of spiritual infection where ever they thrive, while the Kindred literally have no idea anything is going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25885-ozymandias242","name":"Ozymandias242","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T09:53:15-07:00","id":1382989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of