er what a way of doing it would be that was NOT a completely racist shitshow?<br /> <br /> One argument I have is the Ravnos Antediluvian destroying a million lives and utterly decimating the Spirit World with the Week of Nightmares makes the issue of Kindred a MASSIVE one so the Great Leap Outward is an attempt to destroy a threat to the entire world in preparation for Gehenna. However, after the Battle of California, the Kuei-Jin find out the vast majority of vampires have NO IDEA about what the fuck happened themselves. This version of the Kuei-Jin are attempting to destroy Cainites because they believe that the World is Going to EndTM because of them and have a pretty good argument that it's right. However, like the Sabbat, they're aimed at the wrong enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T23:44:30-07:00","id":1383105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383006#post1383006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is one way to play it.<br /> <br /> I wonder what a way of doing it would be that was NOT a completely racist shitshow?<br /> <br /> One argument I have is the Ravnos Antediluvian destroying a million lives and utterly decimating the Spirit World with the Week of Nightmares makes the issue of Kindred a MASSIVE one so the Great Leap Outward is an attempt to destroy a threat to the entire world in preparation for Gehenna. However, after the Battle of California, the Kuei-Jin find out the vast majority of vampires have NO IDEA about what the fuck happened themselves. This version of the Kuei-Jin are attempting to destroy Cainites because they believe that the World is Going to EndTM because of them and have a pretty good argument that it's right. However, like the Sabbat, they're aimed at the wrong enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be funny if the Kue-Jin got here expecting a slavering horde of alien vampires dedicated to destroying the world, and were baffled to discover a bunch of idiots more concerned with avenging that time 50 years ago when someone insulted their favorite painting, or their clothing choices, or just keeping control over the juiciest section of the red light district.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T03:57:13-07:00","id":1383115,"title":"","content":"There's a hilarious Aaron Spelling show from the early 90's, based on what Vampire: the Masquerade was at the time. It's typical prime time evening soap opera material, because that's what Spelling got rich writing and producing, and it's pure schlock. There's a Romeo and Juliet couple who can't be together anymore because the girl was embraced into a different clan than the boyfriend. There's a Nosferatu who experiments with chemicals in the hopes of looking like the male model on a romance novel cover. The Brujah are the bad guys in their feud with the Ventrue, for no clear reason other than that the Ventrue are rich and the problems of rich people are what matter in this genre of television. <br /> <br /> The thought of the Kuei Jin arriving and finding these people running San Francisco makes me howl with laughter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 04-22-2020, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T05:39:08-07:00","id":1383130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383115#post1383115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a hilarious Aaron Spelling show from the early 90's, based on what Vampire: the Masquerade was at the time. It's typical prime time evening soap opera material, because that's what Spelling got rich writing and producing, and it's pure schlock. There's a Romeo and Juliet couple who can't be together anymore because the girl was embraced into a different clan than the boyfriend. There's a Nosferatu who experiments with chemicals in the hopes of looking like the male model on a romance novel cover. The Brujah are the bad guys in their feud with the Ventrue, for no clear reason other than that the Ventrue are rich and the problems of rich people are what matter in this genre of television.<br /> <br /> The thought of the Kuei Jin arriving and finding these people running San Francisco makes me howl with laughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually is kind of hilarious that the Kuei Jin and Kindred have opposite design philosophies.<br /> <br /> Wan Kuei: I am a damned soul brought back in life to fight the Akuma and forces of Hell as part of a second chance. What is your purpose?<br /> <br /> Toreador: Hang out at the Succubus Club, avoid the Prince's wrath, screw mortals for blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T09:42:40-07:00","id":1383152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383115#post1383115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a hilarious Aaron Spelling show from the early 90's, based on what Vampire: the Masquerade was at the time. It's typical prime time evening soap opera material, because that's what Spelling got rich writing and producing, and it's pure schlock. There's a Romeo and Juliet couple who can't be together anymore because the girl was embraced into a different clan than the boyfriend. There's a Nosferatu who experiments with chemicals in the hopes of looking like the male model on a romance novel cover. The Brujah are the bad guys in their feud with the Ventrue, for no clear reason other than that the Ventrue are rich and the problems of rich people are what matter in this genre of television.<br /> <br /> The thought of the Kuei Jin arriving and finding these people running San Francisco makes me howl with laughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindred: The Embraced","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T09:47:50-07:00","id":1383154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383130#post1383130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It actually is kind of hilarious that the Kuei Jin and Kindred have opposite design philosophies.<br /> <br /> Wan Kuei: I am a damned soul brought back in life to fight the Akuma and forces of Hell as part of a second chance. What is your purpose?<br /> <br /> Toreador: Hang out at the Succubus Club, avoid the Prince's wrath, screw mortals for blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I see a direct opposition here, but anyway this is perfect, if simplified, depiction of the reasons why I dropped Kindred as soon as I got acquainted with Wan Kuei. Of course I looked behind from time to time for good old 'individualistic emo goth intrigue' and occasional sectarian warfare, but still. KotE offered all of this + so much more.<br /> Again, imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T11:25:24-07:00","id":1383174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383154#post1383154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think I see a direct opposition here, but anyway this is perfect, if simplified, depiction of the reasons why I dropped Kindred as soon as I got acquainted with Wan Kuei. Of course I looked behind from time to time for good old 'individualistic emo goth intrigue' and occasional sectarian warfare, but still. KotE offered all of this + so much more.<br /> Again, imho.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, its a feature and why I don't want to play Kindred of the East or even Werewolf. As a vampire you have the freedom to make your own adventure.<br /> <br /> As a Kindred of the East, you're a slave to a crusade versus having the ability to make your own way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T13:28:12-07:00","id":1383201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383174#post1383174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a vampire you have the freedom to make your own adventure.</div> </div> </div> </div>As with any other splat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a Kindred of the East, you're a slave to a crusade </div> </div> </div>But you are not.<br /> <br /> <br /> Going back to the topic, I'd make a GLO not an instant mission or invasion, or means to combat overpopulation, but a gradual process of more Hungry Dead awakening around the globe and Wan Kuei being forced to spread across the world as guides and teachers, and staying low and subtle at that instead of open hostility. Different factions of Wan Kuei (Quincunx, Uji, Bamboo Princes) would be doing it in different ways and focusin on different regions. I'd even make certain areas of Asia itself being much less hostile to cainites and actually having their own local versions of main clans or bloodlines. For example, Golden Courts or Infinite Thunder certainly don't give two hecks about any Quincunx crusading dogma so they rather welcome contacts and relations with cainites instead of warring them.<br /> <br /> Ravnos war in India is obviously a Searing Wind guerrilla in their quest to combat whatever they deem as would-be Demon Emperor servants (relatives and descendants of Ravana which Ravnos are to them fall squarely under that category). Local courts could be probably quite on the fence about said war as they were fine with the cold war level of relations with Ravnos and other cainites for centuries. Now, some crazy eschatological fanatics are storming in, raising hell and breaking the carefully maintained status quo.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T14:52:16-07:00","id":1383229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383174#post1383174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, its a feature and why I don't want to play Kindred of the East or even Werewolf. As a vampire you have the freedom to make your own adventure.<br /> <br /> As a Kindred of the East, you're a slave to a crusade versus having the ability to make your own way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your a slave to a crusade only if your a young Hungry Ghosts within certain courts of the Qincunx during a very specific time period. If your part of the majority of Hungry Ghosts outside Mainland China you do not give the slightest of fucks about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T15:13:06-07:00","id":1383232,"title":"","content":"I mean good thing vampires don't have any sort of crusade that say controls the direction of a certain type of character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T17:26:10-07:00","id":1383246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383174#post1383174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, its a feature and why I don't want to play Kindred of the East or even Werewolf. As a vampire you have the freedom to make your own adventure.<br /> <br /> As a Kindred of the East, you're a slave to a crusade versus having the ability to make your own way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Devil Tiger Dharma Book expounds on how you are not supposed to be a slave, though. You're supposed to be a super-cool gardener of sin, going where you will and punishing the sinners who fail to resist sampling your goods. Exactly what you're punishing and why is up to you. The other Dharmas are similarly expansive, even for the ones that the Quincunx follows,<br /> <br /> Well, maybe not the Resplendent Cranes. But everyone else, and the Heretical Dharmas, means that there's a broad range of things to do that doesn't involve a crusade. Now if only it didn't have one big bad straight out of D&amp;D and one other that has an extremely odd choice of name for who he is and what he does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T18:19:13-07:00","id":1383258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383246#post1383246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Devil Tiger Dharma Book expounds on how you are not supposed to be a slave, though. You're supposed to be a super-cool gardener of sin, going where you will and punishing the sinners who fail to resist sampling your goods. Exactly what you're punishing and why is up to you. The other Dharmas are similarly expansive, even for the ones that the Quincunx follows,<br /> <br /> Well, maybe not the Resplendent Cranes. But everyone else, and the Heretical Dharmas, means that there's a broad range of things to do that doesn't involve a crusade. Now if only it didn't have one big bad straight out of D&amp;D and one other that has an extremely odd choice of name for who he is and what he does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I clearly overused my words<br /> <br /> I like games that don't have an overarching narrative driving your character forward. When you're a Vampire, there's nothing to do but what you want.<br /> <br /> Not &quot;Stop the Apocalypse.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T18:21:45-07:00","id":1383259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383258#post1383258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I clearly overused my words<br /> <br /> I like games that don't have an overarching narrative driving your character forward. When you're a Vampire, there's nothing to do but what you want.<br /> <br /> Not &quot;Stop the Apocalypse.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically the Hungry Dead aren't out to do that, either. Quite the opposite, really; they're waiting for the world to come crashing down so that they can throw down with even worse fiends than they or otherwise have a freer run of things. Again, except, perhaps, for the Cranes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T18:27:29-07:00","id":1383260,"title":"","content":"I mean, there's a big chunk of Thrashing Dragons who would put the clubbing Toreador to shame in terms of ' just living the life's, I mean their options range from stuff like ' King/Queen of the Jungle, to brothel madam, to housewife/husband and mother/father, to sewer dwelling vigilante, to corporate heavy hitters and a million other things...and that's just one Dharma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T18:29:39-07:00","id":1383261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383259#post1383259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically the Hungry Dead aren't out to do that, either. Quite the opposite, really; they're waiting for the world to come crashing down so that they can throw down with even worse fiends than they or otherwise have a freer run of things. Again, except, perhaps, for the Cranes.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even that's kind of only a driving nightly concern for some Ancestors, your average Running Monkey is going to pay lip service at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T18:32:58-07:00","id":1383262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383246#post1383246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Devil Tiger Dharma Book expounds on how you are not supposed to be a slave, though. You're supposed to be a super-cool gardener of sin, going where you will and punishing the sinners who fail to resist sampling your goods. Exactly what you're punishing and why is up to you. The other Dharmas are similarly expansive, even for the ones that the Quincunx follows,<br /> <br /> Well, maybe not the Resplendent Cranes. But everyone else, and the Heretical Dharmas, means that there's a broad range of things to do that doesn't involve a crusade. Now if only it didn't have one big bad straight out of D&amp;D and one other that has an extremely odd choice of name for who he is and what he does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luckily the game runs pretty well even if you never bother to drop in any details about the Thousand Halls at all except for some vague flashbacks.<br /> <br /> Agreed that research was kinda lacking in quite a few aspects but luckily I've long since done my own and fixed what was broken/wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T19:20:15-07:00","id":1383271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383260#post1383260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there's a big chunk of Thrashing Dragons who would put the clubbing Toreador to shame in terms of ' just living the life's, I mean their options range from stuff like ' King/Queen of the Jungle, to brothel madam, to housewife/husband and mother/father, to sewer dwelling vigilante, to corporate heavy hitters and a million other things...and that's just one Dharma.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I actually find it a useful mental exercise to take a general thing - high school student, working stiff, corporate heavy weight, street person, rural legend, etc. - and figure out how each dharma would fit in it. </span></span></span></div>Honestly, if I was ever going to run KotE again, I'd probably focus entirely on modern Japan (or at least an anime influenced approximation of it), ignoring a lot of the Sino-centric aspects of the game, and having the young ones do their thing while most of the elders are wrapped up in their own affairs and the two meeting only as the overarcing plot advances. But that is just what I would be most interested in doing personally .<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T20:58:09-07:00","id":1383282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383258#post1383258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I clearly overused my words<br /> <br /> I like games that don't have an overarching narrative driving your character forward. When you're a Vampire, there's nothing to do but what you want.<br /> <br /> Not &quot;Stop the Apocalypse.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Stopping the Apocalypse&quot; can be as much in the foreground or background for a Hungry Ghost as getting swept up into the Jyhad can be for a Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4781-neamhan","name":"Neamhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4781_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T22:20:47-07:00","id":1383291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383258#post1383258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I clearly overused my words<br /> <br /> I like games that don't have an overarching narrative driving your character forward. When you're a Vampire, there's nothing to do but what you want.<br /> <br /> Not &quot;Stop the Apocalypse.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I am reminded of the Second Inquisition in 5th edition. The Second Inquisition has has a profound effect on Vampiric society as well as Vampiric unlife in general. However, despite how massive the Second Inquisition's part in the setting is, there are countless other stories you can tell that have nothing to do with the Second Inquisition. All told, &quot;Dodge the Inquisition&quot; doesn't have to be the only overarching narrative driving Vampire characters, and it's only going to matter to a given character if that's the kind of the story that the ST wants to tell. If the ST isn't interested in telling that story, then the Second Inquisition is going to be of tertiary importance, just something to set the mood or the tone with its occasional mention, but it won't intrude any more than that and won't be central to anyone's storyline.<br /> <br /> In the same way, &quot;Stop the Yama Kings from Turning the Wheel to the 6th Age&quot; is only going to matter insofar as a given ST wants it to matter for their chronicle. And if they want to tell other stories, there are plenty of stories they can tell, while only occasionally using the ideas of an eventual Apocalypse for theme or mood. Really, it fills a pretty similar story niche that Gehenna did in older versions of VtM - it's a world ending apocalypse, but it doesn't have to be the central story to every game.<br /> <br /> I'd argue Werewolf the Apocalypse is a bit more shoehorned into making &quot;Stop the Apocalypse&quot; a central narrative driving characters but even then there are countless types of characters you can make or stories the ST can tell in which that isn't the central narrative either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-23-2020, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T12:12:41-07:00","id":1383417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379442-so-lets-make-the-great-leap-outwards-make-sense?p=1383291#post1383291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am reminded of the Second Inquisition in 5th edition. The Second Inquisition has has a profound effect on Vampiric society as well as Vampiric unlife in general. However, despite how massive the Second Inquisition's part in the setting is, there are countless other stories you can tell that have nothing to do with the Second Inquisition. All told, &quot;Dodge the Inquisition&quot; doesn't have to be the only overarching narrative driving Vampire characters, and it's only going to matter to a given character if that's the kind of the story that the ST wants to tell. If the ST isn't interested in telling that story, then the Second Inquisition is going to be of tertiary importance, just something to set the mood or the tone with its occasional mention, but it won't intrude any more than that and won't be central to anyone's storyline.<br /> <br /> In the same way, &quot;Stop the Yama Kings from Turning the Wheel to the 6th Age&quot; is only going to matter insofar as a given ST wants it to matter for their chronicle. And if they want to tell other stories, there are plenty of stories they can tell, while only occasionally using the ideas of an eventual Apocalypse for theme or mood. Really, it fills a pretty similar story niche that Gehenna did in older versions of VtM - it's a world ending apocalypse, but it doesn't have to be the central story to every game.<br /> <br /> I'd argue Werewolf the Apocalypse is a bit more shoehorned into making &quot;Stop the Apocalypse&quot; a central narrative driving characters but even then there are countless types of characters you can make or stories the ST can tell in which that isn't the central narrative either.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps that &quot;Stop the Apocalypse&quot; is an incredibly broad, multi-faceted goal that requires a lot of different kinds of efforts, some of which might not even be apparent as noteworthy at the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}